{UTF-8}
{ Chapter 23 (from chapter 2's growth model, with a restartable stock and a demand drop for drift tests): a contractor whose crews grow by reinvesting margin, in a region with a steady flow of projects. }
Base Demand=
	50
	~	projects/month
	~	Projects the region produces each month before any change.
	|
Demand Drop=
	0
	~	projects/month
	~	Fall in regional demand from Drop Time on (0: no change).
	|
Drop Time=
	48
	~	month
	~	Month in which demand falls.
	|
Regional Demand=
	Base Demand - STEP(Demand Drop, Drop Time)
	~	projects/month
	~	Projects the region offers each month.
	|
Productivity=
	2
	~	projects/crew/month
	~	Projects a crew completes per month when work is plentiful.
	|
Crew Capacity=
	Crews * Productivity
	~	projects/month
	~	|
Utilisation=
	1 / (1 + (Crew Capacity / Regional Demand)^4)
	~	dmnl
	~	Share of crew time that finds work: near 1 while capacity is well below demand, one half when capacity equals demand, falling steeply beyond.
	|
Projects Done=
	Crew Capacity * Utilisation
	~	projects/month
	~	|
Perception Delay=
	0.25
	~	month
	~	Time for management to see that work is getting scarce.
	|
Perceived Utilisation=
	SMOOTH3(Utilisation, Perception Delay)
	~	dmnl
	~	|
Crews per Project=
	0.08
	~	crew/project
	~	New crews funded by the margin on each project completed.
	|
Crew Additions=
	Crew Capacity * Perceived Utilisation * Crews per Project
	~	crew/month
	~	Crews hired from reinvested margin, judged at the utilisation management believes.
	|
Crew Life=
	24
	~	month
	~	Average time a crew stays.
	|
Crew Departures=
	Crews / Crew Life
	~	crew/month
	~	|
Crews= INTEG(
	Crew Additions - Crew Departures,
	Initial Crews)
	~	crew
	~	|
Initial Crews=
	2
	~	crew
	~	Crews at the start of the run: in operation, the latest count.
	|
INITIAL TIME = 0 ~ month ~ |
FINAL TIME = 72 ~ month ~ |
TIME STEP = 0.0625 ~ month ~ |
SAVEPER = 0.0625 ~ month ~ |
